{title: 369 - Bringing in the Sheaves}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #369 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 369}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Sowing in the morning, sowing seeds of [Gm]kindness,
[Bb]Sowing in the noontide and the [F]dewy eve,
[Bb/F]Waiting for the harvest and the time of [Gm]reaping –
[Bb]We shall come [F]rejoicing, [Bb]bringing in the sheaves.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Bb/F]Bringing in the sheaves, bringing in the sheaves,
[Bb]We shall come [F]rejoicing, [Bb/F]bringing in [Cm]the sheaves.
[Bb/F]Bringing in the sheaves, bringing in the sheaves,
[Bb]We shall come [F]rejoicing, [Bb]bringing in the sheaves.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Sowing in the sunshine, sowing in the [Gm]shadows,
[Bb]Fearing neither clouds nor winter's [F]chilling breeze;
[Bb/F]By and by the harvest and the labor [Gm]ended -
[Bb]We shall come [F]rejoicing, [Bb]bringin in the sheaves.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Going forth with weeping, sowing for the Master,
[Bb]Tho the loss sustained our spirit often [F]grieves;
[Bb/F]When our weeping's over He will bid us [Gm]welcome -
[Bb]We shall come [F]rejoicing, [Bb]bringing in the sheaves
{end_of_verse}
